WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.200
South Africa is dealing with a lot of

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.520
problems — the legacy of apartheid,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.479
huge economic inequality, crushing

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.720
unemployment

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:26.720
and the most recorded cases of COVID-19

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.680
in Africa. But none of that — 

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:32.159
except for the pandemic — is new. So why

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.840
did things kick off back in early July?

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:35.360
Well, you can't answer that question

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.920
without talking about the former

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.640
president,

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.920
Jacob Zuma. He was in office from 2009 to

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.320
2018, 

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:46.720
a time marked by corruption and cronyism

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.720
at the highest levels of government.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.399
Zuma was forced to resign in 2018

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.040
because of all the allegations against

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:52.720
him.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.720
He's been fighting them ever since and

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.280
denies he did anything wrong,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.520
which brings us to the Zondo commission.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.840
It's a public inquiry into what's called

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.200
state capture during Zuma's presidency,

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.520
meaning corruption involving the

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.910
government and the private sector.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.760
Hundreds of

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:19.680
witnesses have provided lots of details

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.599
about what allegedly went on.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.599
President Ramaphosa says the cost of

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:26.080
corruption during Zuma's time in office

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:27.440
was more than $30 billion. 

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.680
So that's some of the backstory. Here's

00:02:40.239 --> 00:02:43.680
how things escalated.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.599
In February this year Zuma refused to

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.840
appear before the Zondo commission — 

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:49.519
even though he testified before. And then

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:51.680
in June the Constitutional Court

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:53.040
sentenced Zuma to 15 months in prison

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.959
for contempt of court.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.800
He was given a deadline to turn himself

00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:59.040
in and at the very last minute

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.080
he showed up at a police station. 

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:29.519
While all that

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.519
was going on

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:32.640
hundreds of Zuma supporters, some

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:34.879
carrying weapons,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.280
rallied in KwaZulu-Natal, his home

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:37.280
province.

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:51.200
And for a while there things did get out

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.200
of hand.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.840
Over the next week there were more than

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.080
300 reported incidents,

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.439
including looting and arson across the

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.000
provinces of

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:03.519
Natal and Gauteng, where the cities of

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.480
Johannesburg, Pretoria

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:08.400
and Durban are. In some places police

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.000
failed to control the looting.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.760
People took security into their own

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.799
hands, from taxi drivers

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.400
to armed vigilantes. President Ramaphosa

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:19.199
was criticised for being too

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.759
slow to act. Eventually, after almost a

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:23.120
week,

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.320
he sent in 25,000 soldiers — the biggest

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.560
military deployment

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.720
since the end of apartheid. And that

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.040
helped to calm things down.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:34.000
And now South Africans have been left to

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.000
clean up the mess.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.800
Well, some of it appeared to be plain

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.360
opportunism. 

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.880
But a lot of people in South

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:39.840
Africa

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:39.840
are struggling to survive.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.479
The World Bank says it's the most

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.639
unequal country

00:05:52.479 --> 00:05:55.520
in the world. Unemployment among young

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:59.039
people stands

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.160
at 75% and the pandemic has made

00:05:59.039 --> 00:06:03.280
everything worse.

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:20.080
That context, though, doesn't

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:22.000
necessarily

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:24.000
explain everything that's happened and

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.919
President Ramaphosa suggested there was

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:29.039
actually something else going on.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:39.680
So that takes it to a

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.680
whole other level.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:43.440
The implication is that Zuma, or people

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.240
close to him, had something to do with

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.479
the violence.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.240
But right now that hasn't been proven

00:06:46.479 --> 00:06:50.240
and as of July 19

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.759
only one suspected ringleader had been

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.840
arrested. Now remember

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:54.880
Ramaphosa and Zuma are from the same

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:57.360
political party —

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:58.000
the ANC — which has run South Africa for

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.039
almost

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.720
30 years, since the end of apartheid. But

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:05.199
the two men now represent

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.880
rival factions within the same party.

00:07:59.599 --> 00:08:03.440
That's one theory and apart from

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:05.680
anything else it shows just how

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.680
complicated this whole situation is.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:09.039
What happened has revealed a lot about

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:10.800
South Africa's problems

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:12.080
and how much work it will take to solve

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.960
them. But it's

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:16.960
also a moment for reflection. 

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.959
For more on the situation in South

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.640
Africa head over to aljazeera.com.

